# Three fields need confirming before the 1.3.2 release is tagged:
#   - date-released: currently set to the day this file was written, not to an actual
#     release date.
#   - identifiers: the Zenodo DOI is commented out below. The README badge image and its
#     link currently point at two different records (…20284071 and …20284070), so the
#     correct concept DOI has to be established first.
#   - preferred-citation: the manuscript is not yet published. Uncomment and complete the
#     block at the end once it is, and update README.md, which currently reads
#     "[citation details will be added upon publication]".

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExP Heatmap in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "ExP Heatmap"
abstract: >-
  Ordered-pair workflow for regional cross-population genomic visualization.
  ExP Heatmap takes a VCF through filter, prepare, compute and plot, and renders
  ordered population-pair matrices as empirical rank-score heatmaps, preserving
  genomic position and reciprocal population-pair direction in a single view.
type: software
version: "1.3.2"
date-released: 2026-07-31
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bioinfocz/exp_heatmap"
url: "https://github.com/bioinfocz/exp_heatmap"

authors:
